        "dependency_level": 3,
        "statement": "Let $G(z,\\theta)$ be $C^2$ near $(z_*,\\theta_0)$, with $z_*=G(z_*,\\theta_0)$. Let $D$ be an open convex state neighborhood of $z_*$ on which $G$ is defined and $C^2$ near $D\\times\\{\\theta_0\\}$. Assume $G(D,\\theta_0)\\subseteq D$, $\\|G_z(z,\\theta_0)\\|\\le q<1$, and $G_z,G_\\theta$ are Lipschitz in $z$ with constants $L_z,L_\\theta$. Let the initial map $z_0(\\theta)$ be $C^1$ and its iterates remain in $D$. Write $s_*=D\\phi(\\theta_0)$ for the local exact fixed-point branch supplied by the implicit function theorem, $e_k=D_\\theta z_k(\\theta_0)$, $\\delta_0=\\|z_0(\\theta_0)-z_*\\|$, $d_0=\\|e_0-s_*\\|$, and $C=L_z\\|s_*\\|+L_\\theta$. For every integer $K\\ge1$,\n$$\\|z_K(\\theta_0)-z_*\\|\\le q^K\\delta_0,\\qquad \\|e_K-s_*\\|\\le q^K d_0+C K q^{K-1}\\delta_0,$$\nwith $q^0=1$ when $q=0,K=1$. If $R(z,\\theta)=z-G(z,\\theta)$ and $r_K=R(z_K(\\theta_0),\\theta_0)$, then $(1-q)\\|z_K-z_*\\|\\le\\|r_K\\|$. The derivative error is not bounded by the residual alone: for $G(z,\\theta)=qz+(1-q)\\theta$, $\\theta_0=0$, and $z_0(\\theta)=0$, every finite $K$ has residual zero at $\\theta_0$ but $e_K=1-q^K\\ne1=s_*$ when $0<q<1$.",
