        "strategy": "1.1 The row inequalities are $5>1$ and $4>1$. Direct multiplication gives $A(5/19,13/19)^T=(2,3)^T$, so the displayed vector is the exact solution. [given, algebra]\n\n2.1 By [F1], $G_J=-D^{-1}(A-D)=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-1/5\\\\-1/4&0\\end{pmatrix}$, whose characteristic polynomial is $\\lambda^2-1/20$. Thus $\\rho(G_J)=1/\\sqrt{20}<1$; [L1] gives convergence from every initial vector to the verified solution. [F1, L1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎",
