      {
        "id": "lem-linear-multistep-order-conditions-from-taylor",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Taylor moment conditions characterize the order of a linear multistep method",
        "deps": [
          "def-linear-multistep-method-consistency-order-and-root-condition",
          "thm-multivariable-taylor-formula-with-lagrange-remainder"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "statement": "For the method in [[def-linear-multistep-method-consistency-order-and-root-condition]], define\n\n$$\\mu_0=\\sum_{j=0}^k\\alpha_j,\\qquad \\mu_m=\\sum_{j=0}^k\\alpha_jj^m-m\\sum_{j=0}^k\\beta_jj^{m-1}\\quad(m\\ge1).$$\n\nFor every integer $p\\ge1$, the method has order at least $p$ if and only if $\\mu_m=0$ for each $m=0,\\ldots,p$. In particular, consistency is equivalent to $\\rho(1)=0$ and $\\rho'(1)=\\sigma(1)$.",
