      {
        "id": "lem-variable-step-bdf2-interpolation-and-local-defect",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Quadratic interpolation gives the variable-step BDF2 formula and cubic residual",
        "deps": [
          "def-linear-multistep-method-consistency-order-and-root-condition",
          "thm-multivariable-taylor-formula-with-lagrange-remainder",
          "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "statement": "Let $h_{n-1},h_n>0$, $r_n=h_n/h_{n-1}$, and let $y$ be an exact solution with three continuous derivatives near $t_{n-1},t_n,t_{n+1}$, where $h_j=t_{j+1}-t_j$. The derivative at $t_{n+1}$ of the quadratic interpolant through $(t_{n+1},y_{n+1})$, $(t_n,y_n)$, and $(t_{n-1},y_{n-1})$ is\n\n$$\\frac{(1+2r_n)y_{n+1}-(1+r_n)^2y_n+r_n^2y_{n-1}}{h_n(1+r_n)}.$$\n\nEquating this derivative to $f(t_{n+1},Y_{n+1})$ defines the variable-step BDF2 formula\n\n$$\\frac{(1+2r_n)Y_{n+1}-(1+r_n)^2Y_n+r_n^2Y_{n-1}}{h_n(1+r_n)}=f(t_{n+1},Y_{n+1}).$$\n\nFor an exact vector solution $y'=f(t,y)$ whose third derivative is bounded, the unscaled residual\n\n$$\\tau_n=(1+2r_n)y(t_{n+1})-(1+r_n)^2y(t_n)+r_n^2y(t_{n-1})-h_n(1+r_n)y'(t_{n+1})$$\n\nhas norm $\\|\\tau_n\\|_\\infty=O(h_n^3)$ uniformly whenever $r_n$ stays in a fixed compact subinterval of $(0,\\infty)$; the formula and remainder hold componentwise.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
