      {
        "id": "alg-variable-step-bdf2-with-selected-implicit-branch",
        "kind": "algorithm",
        "title": "Variable-step BDF2 with an explicit local implicit-branch rule",
        "deps": [
          "def-linear-multistep-method-consistency-order-and-root-condition",
          "lem-variable-step-bdf2-interpolation-and-local-defect",
          "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Input a vector field $f(t,y)$, a finite strictly increasing grid $t_0<\\cdots<t_N$, starting states $Y_0,Y_1\\in\\mathbb R^d$ (so $N\\ge1$), and for each later step a prescribed closed ball $B_{n+1}\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ that specifies the admissible implicit branch. Set $h_n=t_{n+1}-t_n$ and $r_n=h_n/h_{n-1}$ for $1\\le n<N$. If a time increment is nonpositive or the starting dimensions do not agree, return `invalid-grid` or `invalid-input`.\n\nFor $n=1,\\ldots,N-1$, form the equation\n\n$$\\frac{(1+2r_n)Z-(1+r_n)^2Y_n+r_n^2Y_{n-1}}{h_n(1+r_n)}=f(t_{n+1},Z).$$\n\nIf this equation has exactly one root $Z$ in $B_{n+1}$, set $Y_{n+1}=Z$ and continue. If it has no root there, return `no-root` with the computed prefix; if it has more than one root there, return `ambiguous-branch` with the computed prefix. If an evaluation of $f$ is undefined, return `evaluation-failure` with the prefix. On reaching $N$, return `completed` and $(Y_0,\\ldots,Y_N)$. The procedure is defined for arbitrary positive adjacent step ratios; no convergence or accuracy property is part of this algorithm.\n\nThe coefficients are those obtained from the quadratic interpolation derivative in [[lem-variable-step-bdf2-interpolation-and-local-defect]]. A separate theorem gives the uniform ratio hypotheses needed for second-order convergence; they are not part of this algorithm.",
