      {
        "id": "thm-variable-step-bdf2-order-two-under-ratio-bound",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Variable-step BDF2 is second-order convergent under a uniform ratio bound",
        "deps": [
          "alg-variable-step-bdf2-with-selected-implicit-branch",
          "lem-variable-step-bdf2-interpolation-and-local-defect",
          "lem-variable-step-bdf2-increment-ratio-recurrence",
          "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 4,
        "statement": "Let $y'=f(t,y)$ on $[0,T]$, with $y:[0,T]\\to\\mathbb R^d$ having three continuous derivatives. Let $K\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be compact with $y([0,T])\\subset\\operatorname{int}K$, and suppose $f$ is defined on $[0,T]\\times K$ and Lipschitz in its state variable there with constant $L$ in the max norm. Let $h_n=t_{n+1}-t_n>0$, $t_0=0$, $t_N=T$, $H=\\max_n h_n\\to0$, and suppose\n\n$$0<r_{\\min}\\le r_n:=\\frac{h_n}{h_{n-1}}\\le r_*<1+\\sqrt2\\qquad(1\\le n<N).$$\n\nAssume $\\|Y_0-y(t_0)\\|_\\infty+\\|Y_1-y(t_1)\\|_\\infty=O(H^2)$. For each step prescribe a closed branch ball $B_{n+1}\\subset K$ as in [[alg-variable-step-bdf2-with-selected-implicit-branch]], and suppose that for every pair of preceding states in $K$ the step equation has exactly one root in $B_{n+1}$. Select that root. Then for sufficiently small $H$ all computed states remain in $K$ and\n\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|Y_n-y(t_n)\\|_\\infty=O(H^2).$$\n\nThe lower ratio bound controls the local residual constant; the upper bound controls the parasitic increment. This is a separate variable-grid theorem and does not follow from the constant-step root condition alone.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "justified_by": [],
        "sources": {
