      {
        "id": "lem-second-order-jet-on-a-regular-level-set",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "A regular level set realizes every compatible second-order jet",
        "deps": [
          "thm-differential-rank-is-lower-semicontinuous",
          "cor-regular-level-set-local-graph-theorem",
          "cor-second-order-taylor-expansion-with-the-hessian"
        ],
        "statement": "Let $H:U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^q$ be $C^2$, let $x\\in U$, and\nsuppose $DH(x)$ is surjective. If $d\\in\\ker DH(x)$ and\n$$DH(x)z+D^2H(x)[d,d]=0,$$\nthen there is a $C^2$ curve $\\gamma$ on the level $H=H(x)$ near $0$ with\n$\\gamma(0)=x$, $\\gamma'(0)=d$, and $\\gamma''(0)=z$. For $q=0$ the level is\nall of $U$ and the statement is immediate.",
        "strategy": "1.1 If $q=0$, then $H$ is the unique map into $\\mathbb R^0$ and the level is all of $U$. The curve $\\gamma(t)=x+td+\\tfrac12t^2z$ has the required value and first two derivatives. [given, construct]\n\n1.2 Now suppose $q>0$ and take the graph in [F1]. Put $v=D^2\\psi(0)[d,d]$. Since $H(x+td+\\psi(td))=H(x)$ for small $t$, [F2] and $\\psi(td)=\\tfrac12t^2v+o(t^2)$ give $DH(x)d=0$ and $DH(x)v+D^2H(x)[d,d]=0$. [F1, F2, given, algebra]\n\n2.1 The compatibility equation for $z$ and step 1.2 imply $e=z-v\\in\\ker DH(x)$. Define $u(t)=td+\\tfrac12t^2e$ and $\\gamma(t)=x+u(t)+\\psi(u(t))$. This curve stays on $H=H(x)$ by [F1]. Using [F2] and $D\\psi(0)=0$ gives $\\gamma(t)=x+td+\\tfrac12t^2(e+v)+o(t^2) =x+td+\\tfrac12t^2z+o(t^2)$, so its first two derivatives at $0$ are $d$ and $z$. [step 1.2, F1, F2, construct] ∎",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Boyd and Vandenberghe, Convex Optimization",
