        "id": "alg-saga-finite-sum-method",
        "kind": "algorithm",
        "title": "Finite-sum SAGA",
        "statement": "Let n,d>=1, let f_1,...,f_n:R^d->R be continuously differentiable, and set F(x)=n^{-1}sum_i f_i(x), with \\nabla F(x)=n^{-1}sum_i\\nabla f_i(x) by [[lem-finite-sum-gradient-is-average]] and [[def-finite-sum]]. Given a deterministic initial point x_0 and step size \\eta>0, initialize a table \\alpha_i^0=\\nabla f_i(x_0) and its mean \\bar\\alpha_0=n^{-1}sum_i\\alpha_i^0. At iteration k:\n\n1. Draw I_k uniformly from {1,...,n}, independently of the history \\mathcal F_k.\n2. Using the old table, form\n   $$\n   v_k=\\nabla f_{I_k}(x_k)-\\alpha_{I_k}^k+\\bar\\alpha_k,\\qquad x_{k+1}=x_k-\\eta v_k.\n   $$\n3. Replace only the sampled table entry, using the pre-update point:\n   $$\n   \\alpha_{I_k}^{k+1}=\\nabla f_{I_k}(x_k),\\qquad \\alpha_i^{k+1}=\\alpha_i^k\\quad(i\\ne I_k),\n   $$\n   and set\n   $$\n   \\bar\\alpha_{k+1}=\\bar\\alpha_k+\\frac1n\\big(\\nabla f_{I_k}(x_k)-\\alpha_{I_k}^k\\big).\n   $$\n\nInitialization uses n component-gradient evaluations. Each later iteration uses one new component gradient and O(d) arithmetic if the running table mean is maintained. The table stores n gradients, so storage is O(nd). For each fixed history the correction is a finite control-variate estimator of the form in [[def-control-variate-estimator]]; the conditional claims are proved locally. The conditional-expectation convention inherits [[def-axiom-of-choice]] from [[def-stochastic-gradient-oracle-and-unconstrained-update]].\n",
